# Specific Engineering Instructions
1. Implement the requested component/module using clean, idiomatic code adhering strictly to the tech stack versions.
2. Provide complete type annotations, docstrings (Google or Sphinx style), and comprehensive error handling.
3. Keep business logic strictly decoupled from presentation or database drivers.
4. Include input validation and boundary condition guards.

# Constraints & Rules
- Do NOT use placeholder comments like `// TODO: implement later` or `pass` in critical business logic.
- Avoid introducing undeclared third-party dependencies.
- Ensure all public functions and classes have explicit type hints.

